# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# RO. Nation LIVE - environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public base URL of the site (no trailing slash). Used for OAuth redirects & links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ---- Database (Postgres) -----------------------------------------
# This value is used when you run the app on your machine (`npm run dev`) and by
# the `prisma` CLI. Port 5433 is where docker-compose.override.yml publishes the
# local Postgres container.
# Inside Docker the web container ignores this and talks to `db:5432` directly.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ronation:ronation@localhost:5433/ronation?schema=public"

# ---- Sessions & security -----------------------------------------
# Long random string used to sign session cookies. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
AUTH_SECRET="change-me-to-a-long-random-string"

# NOTE: ADMIN_USERNAME and ADMIN_PASSWORD are GONE. The shared-password /admin
# dashboard was merged into /company, which ranks off the Roblox group below -
# access is per-person, revoked by demotion rather than by rotating a secret
# several people knew, and every write is attributable to an account. If those
# two are still in your .env, delete them; nothing reads them.

# ---- Roblox OAuth 2.0 (OpenID Connect) ---------------------------
# Create an app at https://create.roblox.com/dashboard/credentials
# Scopes to enable: openid profile
#
# Register exactly ONE redirect URL:
#
#   https://authorise.ronation.live/api/auth/roblox/callback
#
# And the local-dev equivalent - note it is the authorise host there too, so that
# dev exercises the real cross-host handoff rather than a same-origin shortcut that
# would hide bugs:
#   http://authorise.localhost:3000/api/auth/roblox/callback
#
# On Windows, .localhost names do not resolve on their own: add authorise.localhost
# to your hosts file, alongside whatever you already added for the partner hosts.
#
# That is the whole list, and it does not grow. Every other host - the portal, the
# survey site, every partner - signs people in by sending them to
# authorise.ronation.live and taking back a short-lived ticket (src/lib/sso.ts).
# None of them ever speaks to Roblox, so none of them needs a redirect URL here.
#
# It used to be one entry per host, which meant a new subdomain was a change in the
# Roblox OAuth app as well as in DNS - and forgetting it broke sign-in on exactly
# one host while every other host kept working, which is the sort of failure that
# ships. Adding a subdomain is now: a DNS record, a name on the Caddyfile address
# line, and an entry in knownOrigins() in src/lib/sso.ts.
ROBLOX_CLIENT_ID=""
ROBLOX_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# These default to Roblox's public endpoints - only change if Roblox moves them.
ROBLOX_AUTHORIZE_URL="https://apis.roblox.com/oauth/v1/authorize"
ROBLOX_TOKEN_URL="https://apis.roblox.com/oauth/v1/token"
ROBLOX_USERINFO_URL="https://apis.roblox.com/oauth/v1/userinfo"

# ---- In-game API key: the ROOT key --------------------------------
# Secret shared with your Roblox game so it can verify/redeem tickets over HTTP.
# Send it as the `x-api-key` header. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
#
# THIS IS NO LONGER THE ONLY KEY, AND IT IS THE MOST DANGEROUS ONE.
#
# Keys are now rows in the database, minted in the portal (portal.ronation.live/
# <org>/keys). A minted key belongs to ONE organisation and carries only the scopes
# it was given, so a partner's key can reach a partner's shows and nothing else,
# and a door scanner cannot issue tickets.
#
# This env var is the key that predates all of that, and it is deliberately
# unchanged: it is UNSCOPED (every org's shows, RNL's and every partner's) and it
# holds EVERY capability - verify, redeem, issue, gift, purchase, void, revoke. It
# stays because it is live in RNL's game servers today and narrowing it would take
# the door down on deploy. It cannot be revoked from the portal, only unset here.
#
# It should not outlive the migration. Mint a scoped key at /shasha/keys, move the
# game servers onto it, then delete this line. Leaving it set is leaving a skeleton
# key under the mat.
#
# Leave it EMPTY and it is simply off - every caller must then hold a minted key.
GAME_API_KEY="change-me-to-a-long-random-string"

# ---- Paid tickets in Robux (OFF) ----------------------------------
# The master switch for charging Robux for a ticket. Leave this false.
#
# Events can already have PAID TIERS - a partner (Sleep Token, say) can set up
# "VIP - Front Barrier, 250 R$" in their portal right now. With this off, that
# tier shows at checkout as locked, priced, and unbuyable, and the reserve action
# refuses to issue one even if the form is forged. That is the intended state.
#
# Do NOT flip this to "true" just to make the button work. Robux cannot be
# charged from a website: a real payment is a Developer Product prompted inside
# the Roblox experience, which Roblox confirms by calling ProcessReceipt on YOUR
# game server. Turning this on before that exists means selling tickets that
# nothing collects money for.
#
# The RECEIVING END now exists: POST /api/v1/tickets/purchase, called from
# ProcessReceipt, idempotent on the receipt's PurchaseId. What does not exist -
# and cannot, because Roblox offers no server-to-server receipt check - is any way
# for us to VERIFY that a payment happened. We take the game server's word for it.
# Read the note at the top of src/app/api/v1/tickets/purchase/route.ts before you
# switch this on; it is the one place in this system that trusts a caller.
#
# To actually switch paid ticketing on, all of this has to be true:
#   1. A Developer Product exists on the experience, per paid tier.
#   2. The game server's ProcessReceipt handler calls /api/v1/tickets/purchase,
#      passing receipt.PurchaseId, and grants only on `issued: true`.
#   3. It calls with a key holding the TICKETS_PURCHASE scope - and that key is on
#      a game server you would trust with your own Robux, because it can mint paid
#      tickets for free.
#   4. The partner is allowed to price in Robux - `robuxTickets: true` on their
#      entry in src/lib/partners/registry.ts. This env var alone is not enough;
#      it takes both keys. See robuxSalesAllowed() in src/lib/tickets/pricing.ts.
ROBUX_TICKETS_ENABLED="false"

# ---- The rank ladder ----------------------------------------------
# RO. Nation LIVE's Roblox group. EVERY door into the organisation is a rank in
# it: /company, the SHASHA portal, and the override that opens every partner
# portal. There is no allowlist to maintain anywhere - promoting somebody IS the
# grant, demoting them IS the revocation. Rank is re-read from Roblox on each
# request (cached ~5 min), never trusted from the session cookie, so a change
# lands on its own with no config edit and no redeploy.
#
# https://www.roblox.com/communities/33033115/RoNation-Live
ROBLOX_GROUP_ID="33033115"
#
# Roblox ranks run 0–255 (guest 0, owner 255). The thresholds nest:
#
#   200+   SHASHA portal, read only - search the VIP list and the blacklist
#   245+   SHASHA writes, AND /company: all of ronation.live
#   250+   every partner portal and their studio, as an owner-equivalent
#
# The COMPANY_/PARTNERS_/SHASHA_GROUP_ID overrides all default to ROBLOX_GROUP_ID
# above; set one only if the gates ever need to point at different groups.

# ---- The Company (/company) ---------------------------------------
# RNL's own site: events, blog, surveys, careers, applications, attendees. This
# replaced BOTH the old /studio and the password-protected /admin - those two
# paths now just redirect here.
COMPANY_MIN_RANK="245"

# ---- Partner portals (portal.ronation.live/<slug>) ----------------
# Rank this high in RNL's group opens EVERY partner portal and their studio, with
# no PartnerMember row and nothing to revoke by hand.
#
# It is the most powerful grant in the system - the one that reaches into
# organisations RNL does not own - so it deliberately sits at the top of the
# ladder. A partner's own staff get in the other way, via a PartnerMember row
# (see STRO_OWNER_ROBLOX_ID below); they are not in this group at all.
PARTNER_STAFF_RANK="250"

# ---- HTTPS / Caddy (production only) ------------------------------
# The Caddy container terminates TLS and gets Let's Encrypt certificates for
# these hostnames automatically - no certbot, no cron, no renewal script. Each
# must already point at this server in DNS, and ports 80 + 443 must be open.
SITE_HOST="ronation.live"
PORTAL_HOST="portal.ronation.live"
SURVEY_HOST="survey.ronation.live"
# The sign-in host. Every other host sends people here to authenticate, so if this
# name does not resolve, nobody can sign in to ANYTHING - not the portal, not a
# survey, not a partner site. It is the one host to check first when sign-in breaks.
AUTHORISE_HOST="authorise.ronation.live"

# ---- Partner site hosts -------------------------------------------
# One per partner, matching the slug in src/lib/partners/registry.ts. Add the
# host to the Caddyfile's address line too - and only once DNS resolves, or the
# failed Let's Encrypt issuance counts against the 5-per-week limit.
STRO_HOST="sleeptokenro.ronation.live"

# ---- Sleep Token portal owner ----------------------------------
# A slug in the partner registry grants nobody anything: access to
# portal.ronation.live/sleeptokenro is a PartnerMember row, and prisma/seed.ts
# is what creates it. The seed runs on every container boot and upserts this
# Roblox user id as OWNER, so leaving these blank means NOBODY can sign in to
# that portal - the page redirects to /sleeptokenro/login and stops there.
#
# The id is the number in https://www.roblox.com/users/<id>/profile.
#
# This seeds ONE owner. There is no member-management screen yet, so any further
# staff are, for now, PartnerMember rows inserted by hand.
STRO_OWNER_ROBLOX_ID=""
STRO_OWNER_NAME=""

# Let's Encrypt emails this address before a certificate expires. Renewal happens
# automatically regardless - this is just so the warnings reach a real inbox.
ACME_EMAIL="you@example.com"

# ---- SHASHA portal (portal.ronation.live/shasha) ------------------
# Any host starting with "portal." serves the staff portal at /shasha; every
# other path on that host is bounced to the main site, and /shasha on the main
# site is bounced to the portal. On localhost both are served, for dev.
#
# Sign-in is Roblox, and access is your rank in the group above - see the ladder.
#
#   rank >= SHASHA_MIN_RANK      search the VIP list and the blacklist
#   rank >= SHASHA_MANAGER_RANK  add, edit and remove people
#
# NOTE: portal.ronation.live must be registered as a Roblox OAuth redirect URL -
# see the Roblox section above - or staff cannot sign in at all.
SHASHA_MIN_RANK="200"
SHASHA_MANAGER_RANK="245"

# ---- Dev convenience ---------------------------------------------
# When "true" AND Roblox OAuth is not configured, a mock login is enabled so you
# can click through ticketing locally without real Roblox credentials.
# ALWAYS set to "false" in production.
ALLOW_DEV_LOGIN="true"
